        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="true">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal> The few places I found air leaks include the Blaze King combustion air duct, dryer duct, back and upper deck door weatherstripping, window frames in the living room &amp;, Bensons bedroom &amp; the M bedroom &amp; bathroom seals (as if they dont close tightly) and the attic hatch. </airSeal>
                <CoolingSystem>Through the Canada Greener Homes Grant initiative, a grant of $1,000 per KW is available for installing a photovoltaic solar panel. If you choose to install a photovoltaic (PV) system, it is strongly recommended that a full assessment by a professional solar photovoltaic installer, including the measuring of solar irradiance (how much sunlight falls on the roof) is undertaken to provide detailed information on considerations for your home and specific installation recommendations, including the size and related energy production of the system. The rated PV panel must have peak power capacity.



Through the Canada Greener Homes Grant initiative, a grant of $1000 is available for the installation of battery storage and an inverter to connect to a photovoltaic system to provide standby power for the home for an existing PV system or a new install. This resiliency measure must be combined with an energy efficiency retrofit from the Canada Greener Homes Grant in order to be eligible. This grant may be combined with the new PV installation grant for a maximum grant of $5000.</CoolingSystem>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="true" evaluationCost="50">
                <Community>Whitehorse</Community>
            </GreenerHomes>
        </Options>
